# Requests that show OpenIDProviderApp working before any client exists: the discovery
# document, the published keys, an access token from the client credentials grant, and introspection of
# that token.
#
# Start the provider first (dotnet run --project OpenIDProviderApp), then open this file in Visual Studio,
# JetBrains Rider or VS Code (REST Client extension) and send each request in turn. Trust the development
# HTTPS certificate once so the client accepts it:
#     dotnet dev-certs https --trust

# The provider's address: its launch profile's URL, which is also the issuer it writes into every token.
@host = https://localhost:5001

# A confidential client registered for the client credentials grant only; "secret" is the demo
# secret whose SHA-512 hash the provider keeps in appsettings.json.
@clientId = console_client
@clientSecret = secret

# After running the token request below, paste its access_token here to run the introspection request.
@accessToken = paste-the-access_token-here

### Discovery document
# Answers 200 with the issuer https://localhost:5001 and the endpoint addresses used below: token_endpoint,
# jwks_uri and introspection_endpoint.
GET {{host}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

### Published keys
# Answers 200 with the public half of each signing key (kty, n, e), never any private material.
GET {{host}}/.well-known/jwks

### Access token from the client credentials grant
# Answers 200 with access_token, token_type Bearer and expires_in: a token for the client itself.
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}

### Introspection of that token
# The endpoint answers only an authenticated client, so the same client sends its own credentials; the
# token was issued to it, so it needs no further permission. Answers 200 with "active": true and the
# token's client_id and exp; an expired or unknown token answers 200 with "active": false.
POST {{host}}/connect/introspect
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

token={{accessToken}}&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}
